{"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-22","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on the Judiciary, and in addition to the Committee on House Administration, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-10-22","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on the Judiciary, and in addition to the Committee on House Administration, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-10-22","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-10-22","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[],"total":0},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsha00","name":"Committee on House Administration","subcommittees":[]},{"activities":[{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsju00","name":"Judiciary Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":37,"fetched_at":"2026-11-04T22:18:58+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-25","importance":null,"viability":39.3},{"day":"2026-10-27","importance":null,"viability":39.0}],"id":"119-hr-10907","importance":50,"importance_band":"moderate","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":58.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Affects state and local election officials, voters, individuals involved in legal challenges or recounts, and state entities applying for ballot tracking grants.","evidence":"The Commission is authorized to make grants to States to cover costs incurred in establishing and administering qualifying balloting materials tracking programs.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":60},{"assessment":"Significantly alters legal timelines by extending criminal statutes of limitations to 9 years and placing strict judicial constraints on the seizure of ballots and election equipment.","evidence":"No person shall be prosecuted, tried, or punished for any offense under this section unless the indictment is found... not later than 9 years after the date","evidence_verified":false,"key":"magnitude","score":50},{"assessment":"Authorizes an appropriation of $50,000,000 for fiscal year 2027 to fund state balloting materials tracking programs.","evidence":"There are authorized to be appropriated $50,000,000 to the Commission for fiscal year 2027 for payments under this section.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"fiscal","score":40},{"assessment":"Amends multiple federal statutes including the federal criminal code, Voting Rights Act, National Voter Registration Act, Civil Rights Act of 1960, and Help America Vote Act.","evidence":"A person who is aggrieved by a violation of section 592, 593, or 594 of title 18, United States Code, may bring a civil action","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":60},{"assessment":"Establishes permanent changes to federal statutes of limitations, legal rights of action, and election record seizure rules.","evidence":null,"evidence_verified":false,"key":"duration","score":80}],"missing_information":["The exact distribution formula or individual state allocations for the $50 million grant authorization."],"rationale":"The SHIELD Our Elections Act creates a new private right of action for election interference at polling locations, extends the statute of limitations for specified election crimes to 9 years, restricts the seizure of election records and ballots, and authorizes $50 million in grants for state ballot tracking programs.","score":50},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-11-04T22:27:14+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite",